IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part10`

-- Tests for wa-interpretation-part10.l4 (ss 73 to 77, notes 1 and 4) and for the Second Schedule B to E rules in
-- wa-interpretation-time.l4.  Expected values are written from the text.
-- Weekdays, by hand calendar arithmetic: 1 Jan 2025 is a Wednesday, so Wed 15 Jan, Fri 31 Jan, Sat 15 Feb, Mon 17 Feb,
-- Tue 18 Feb, Fri 28 Feb, Mon 10 Mar, Mon 31 Mar, Thu 10 Apr, Tue 15 Apr, Tue 15 Jul 2025; 1 Jan 2026 is a Thursday,
-- so Thu 15 Jan 2026.

§ `Tests -- Part X`

-- s 73
#ASSERT `the day the State is deemed to have been established, for the applicability of Imperial Acts` EQUALS Date 1 6 1829
#ASSERT `the Imperial Act was enacted before the State is deemed to have been established` (Date 31 5 1829)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Imperial Act was enacted before the State is deemed to have been established` (Date 1 6 1829))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Imperial Act was enacted before the State is deemed to have been established` (Date 1 1 1900))

-- s 74: only a deviation that neither affects the substance materially nor is likely to mislead
#ASSERT `the deviation invalidates the form used` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the deviation invalidates the form used` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the deviation invalidates the form used` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the deviation invalidates the form used` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 75(2) and (3)
#ASSERT `service may be effected either by registered post or by certified mail` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `service may be effected either by registered post or by certified mail` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `service may be effected either by registered post or by certified mail` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `service may be effected either by registered post or by certified mail` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `service may be effected either by registered post or by certified mail` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 75(1) applies` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 75(1) applies` TRUE)

-- s 76: each manner, with the person-dependent limbs
#ASSERT `service may be effected in the manner` `delivering the document to the person personally` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `service may be effected in the manner` `post in accordance with section 75(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `service may be effected in the manner` `leaving it at the person's usual or last known place of abode` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `service may be effected in the manner` `leaving it at the usual or last known place of business of a person who is a principal of a business` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `service may be effected in the manner` `leaving it at the usual or last known place of business of a person who is a principal of a business` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `service may be effected in the manner` `delivering, leaving or posting it, addressed to a corporation or association, at its principal place of business or principal office in the State` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `service may be effected in the manner` `delivering, leaving or posting it, addressed to a corporation or association, at its principal place of business or principal office in the State` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `service may be effected in the manner` `some other manner` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a written law that directs a particular manner: the section does not apply
#ASSERT `service may be effected in the manner` `delivering the document to the person personally` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 76A
#ASSERT `the provision has the effect and validity it would have had if the Australia Acts had been in operation then` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the provision has the effect and validity it would have had if the Australia Acts had been in operation then` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `subsection (1) is to be given effect so as to bring it about` `invalidating an enactment that was valid immediately before the commencement of the Australia Acts` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) is to be given effect so as to bring it about` `invalidating an Act because it was assented to by the Sovereign rather than the Governor` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `subsection (1) is to be given effect so as to bring it about` `some other result` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 77(2): Acts passed before 1 July 1984
#ASSERT `section 11 of the Interpretation Act 1918 continues to apply to the Act` (Date 30 6 1984)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 11 of the Interpretation Act 1918 continues to apply to the Act` (Date 1 7 1984))
#ASSERT NOT (`section 11 of the Interpretation Act 1918 continues to apply to the Act` (Date 1 1 2000))
-- s 77(3)
#ASSERT `the enactment is presumed to have amended the law so as to affect the construction of the earlier law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the enactment is presumed to have amended the law so as to affect the construction of the earlier law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the enactment is presumed to have amended the law so as to affect the construction of the earlier law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 77(4)
#ASSERT `section 47(2) and the Second Schedule of the Interpretation Act 1918 continue to apply to the Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 47(2) and the Second Schedule of the Interpretation Act 1918 continue to apply to the Act` FALSE)

-- note 1: section 11 of the 1918 Act
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the exercise may confer a right or impose an obligation before the Act comes into operation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the exercise may confer a right or impose an obligation before the Act comes into operation` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the exercise is deemed as valid and effectual as if section 11 as re-enacted in 1975 had been in operation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the exercise is deemed as valid and effectual as if section 11 as re-enacted in 1975 had been in operation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a reference to an Act in section 11 includes it` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to an Act in section 11 includes it` FALSE)

-- note 4: s 47 and the Second Schedule
#ASSERT `the section of the Second Schedule is incorporated as an enactment in the Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the section of the Second Schedule is incorporated as an enactment in the Act` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the reference is deemed to be to the corresponding section of the Second Schedule to the Interpretation Act 1918` `the Second Schedule to the Interpretation Act 1898` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference is deemed to be to the corresponding section of the Second Schedule to the Interpretation Act 1918` `the Schedule to the Shortening Ordinance 1853` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the reference is deemed to be to the corresponding section of the Second Schedule to the Interpretation Act 1918` `some other schedule` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Act by which section A of the Second Schedule says informations, complaints and proceedings are heard and penalties enforced` EQUALS "Justices Act 1902"
#ASSERT `the proceeding may be quashed, vacated or removed on that ground` `want of form only` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the proceeding may be quashed, vacated or removed on that ground` `removal by certiorari, or by any writ or process whatsoever, into any superior Court of the State` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the proceeding may be quashed, vacated or removed on that ground` `some other ground` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the plaintiff recovers in the action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the plaintiff recovers in the action` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the plaintiff recovers in the action` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the defendant recovers full costs as between solicitor and client` `a verdict passed for the defendant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the defendant recovers full costs as between solicitor and client` `the plaintiff became nonsuited or discontinued after issue joined` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the defendant recovers full costs as between solicitor and client` `judgment was given against the plaintiff upon demurrer or otherwise` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the defendant recovers full costs as between solicitor and client` `a verdict was given for the plaintiff` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the plaintiff who obtained a verdict has costs against the defendant` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the plaintiff who obtained a verdict has costs against the defendant` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an action lies against the defendant` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an action lies against the defendant` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an action lies against the defendant` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an action lies against the defendant` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Court may award the defendant treble costs or such portion of them as it thinks fit` `judgment after verdict for the defendant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Court may award the defendant treble costs or such portion of them as it thinks fit` `judgment by a Judge sitting as a jury for the defendant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Court may award the defendant treble costs or such portion of them as it thinks fit` `judgment on demurrer for the defendant` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Court may award the defendant treble costs or such portion of them as it thinks fit` `the plaintiff discontinued` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Court may award the defendant treble costs or such portion of them as it thinks fit` `the plaintiff became nonsuit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Court may award the defendant treble costs or such portion of them as it thinks fit` `judgment for the plaintiff` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Second Schedule B to E (time module): the time to complain runs from the day AFTER the offence (s 61(1)(b)), by calendar
-- months (s 62), and an end that falls on an excluded day rolls forward (s 61(1)(e)).
GIVETH A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
`part 10 no holidays` MEANS
    `Holidays that make an excluded day` WITH
        `public service holidays`            IS EMPTY
        `bank holidays in the relevant area`   IS EMPTY
        `public holidays in the relevant area` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
`part 10 a public holiday on Monday 17 February 2025` MEANS
    `Holidays that make an excluded day` WITH
        `public service holidays`            IS EMPTY
        `bank holidays in the relevant area`   IS EMPTY
        `public holidays in the relevant area` IS LIST (Date 17 2 2025)

-- B, one month: offence Wed 15 Jan 2025 -> first day 16 Jan -> a month ends 15 Feb (Saturday) -> Monday 17 Feb
#ASSERT `the last day to make the complaint and commence the proceedings` `section B -- one month` (Date 15 1 2025) (`part 10 no holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 17 2 2025)
-- the same with Monday 17 Feb a public holiday -> Tuesday 18 Feb
#ASSERT `the last day to make the complaint and commence the proceedings` `section B -- one month` (Date 15 1 2025) (`part 10 a public holiday on Monday 17 February 2025`) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 2 2025)
-- offence Mon 10 Mar 2025 -> first day 11 Mar -> ends 10 Apr (Thursday)
#ASSERT `the last day to make the complaint and commence the proceedings` `section B -- one month` (Date 10 3 2025) (`part 10 no holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 4 2025)
-- offence Fri 31 Jan 2025 -> first day 1 Feb, the first day of a month -> the month ends 28 Feb (Friday)
#ASSERT `the last day to make the complaint and commence the proceedings` `section B -- one month` (Date 31 1 2025) (`part 10 no holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- offence Fri 28 Feb 2025 -> first day 1 Mar -> ends 31 Mar (Monday)
#ASSERT `the last day to make the complaint and commence the proceedings` `section B -- one month` (Date 28 2 2025) (`part 10 no holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2025)
-- C, three months: offence 15 Jan 2025 -> 16 Jan + 3 months -> 15 Apr (Tuesday)
#ASSERT `the last day to make the complaint and commence the proceedings` `section C -- three months` (Date 15 1 2025) (`part 10 no holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 4 2025)
-- D, six months: -> 15 Jul 2025 (Tuesday)
#ASSERT `the last day to make the complaint and commence the proceedings` `section D -- six months` (Date 15 1 2025) (`part 10 no holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 7 2025)
-- E, twelve months: -> 15 Jan 2026 (Thursday)
#ASSERT `the last day to make the complaint and commence the proceedings` `section E -- twelve months` (Date 15 1 2025) (`part 10 no holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)
-- the Schedule's periods: one, three, six, twelve months
#ASSERT `the period the Second Schedule section allows` `section B -- one month` EQUALS `Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS 1, `unit` IS `in months`
#ASSERT `the period the Second Schedule section allows` `section E -- twelve months` EQUALS `Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS 12, `unit` IS `in months`
